Hi all,

I'm learning about renderUI / uiOutputs with selectInput(), but haven't found an example which addresses my question. (I'll put together a repeatable example this afternoon if requested.)

So, we have two selectInputs rendered dynamically from server.R, one which accepts multiple selections, the other which is restricted to one. This logic needs to be interchangeable, if you will.

That is to say, I need to enforce the rule that
 - when uiOutput("A") has only one element selected,
 - the uiOutput("B") should get "multiple = TRUE" to allow multiple selections.
 - and if the user made multiple selections in uiOutput("A") they should be restricted to one in uiOutput("B").

Is there already an example of this in the amazing archive of Shiny examples? I'm imagining a reactive() section with an isolate call, but I'm quite lost in the implementation.

Thanks very much
Jeff

