Thanks for responding, but I would expect ui1UI to show up until I click on 'confirm', which is not what happens right now. Also, I am confused about two aspects:

1.Why do I return `cond` and not `cond()`? I thought `cond()` would have returned the reactive value, which is all I need in server.R

2. Is   `cond <- callModule(ui1, "ui1")` all I need to call in server.R? How does the `observeEvent` in ui1() get passed to server.R then?

Below the code updated with your corrections:

ui.R

tagList(useShinyjs(), htmlOutput("page"))

server.R

shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {

  cond <- callModule(ui1, "ui1")

  output$page <- renderUI(expr= if(is.null(cond())) {
    ui1UI('ui1')
    } else {
    ui2UI('ui2')
    }

    )
})

ui1.R

ui1UI <-  function(id, label = "ui1UI") {
  ns <- NS(id)
  shinyUI(fluidPage(
    textInput(ns('id'), 'ID'),
    actionButton(ns("confirm"), "Submit", class='btn-primary')

  ))
}

ui1 <- function(input, output, session) {

  cond <- reactive({ input$confirm})

  observeEvent(length(input$id)!="", {
    toggleState("confirm")
  })

  return(cond)

}

ui2.R

ui2UI <-  function(id, label = "ui2UI") {
  ns <- NS(id)
  shinyUI(fluidPage(
    textInput(ns('id'), 'Second Page')

  ))
}

ui2 <- function(input, output, session) {

